        </p>

        <p class="tagline">
          Faith. Service. Compassion.
        </p>

        <p class="intro">
          Saint Teresa of Calcutta—known throughout the world as Mother Teresa—
          dedicated her life to serving people who were poor, sick, abandoned,
          and dying. Her work eventually became known around the world, but it
          began simply: in the streets and slums of Calcutta, caring for
          individuals one person at a time.
        </p>

        <p class="intro">
          Less well known is a fascinating chapter in that history: Mother
          Teresa’s apparent connection with homeopathy.
        </p>

        <p class="intro">
          Some claims about that relationship are difficult to verify through
          surviving primary documents. Others, however, are supported by
          firsthand testimony and institutional records. Together, they reveal
          a story worth exploring—and one that continues to invite historical
          research.
        </p>

      </div>
    </section>

